Davide Inglima - limaCAT <hadesnebula@despammed.com> wrote:
> If I upload my own bones files to Hearse, am I (at least morally) obliged to 
> delete my own bones files?

I have wondered at this myself.

If you want to emulate playing on a multi-user system, then it seems 
that you should delete some, but not all, of your own bones files.

However, a multi-user system with many players might, at any given time, 
have more bones than you would with your bones and the Hearse 
counterparts.  So arguably keeping all of your own bones is similar, in 
terms of the effect of bones on game balance, to playing on a well-used 
public server.

If you want to see others' bones, but want the balance of the game to be 
roughly similar to what it would be if you had only your own bones, 
then you should delete all of your own bones files.

